{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA792230","title":"Microbial analysis effected by NaClO","description":"Sodium hypochlorite (NaClO) is a commonly used chemical to deal with membrane fouling, but it is toxic to microorganisms. Since the toxic effect in the anaerobic reaction is currently unclear, in the long-term experiment, a lower concentration solution is generally used as a membrane cleaning reagent refers to the aerobic reaction process. In this study, effects of NaClO concentration on the biodegradation performance and the microbial activity was investigated at a NaClO concentration range of 0-9 g/L related to the anaerobic membrane bioreactor via batch experiments and the microbial community analysis. In addition, for seeking a way to maintain the performance of the anaerobic digestion process under the impact of high NaClO concentration, a follow-up batch experiment was further implemented.","center":"Tohoku University","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2021/12/25 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN24404847","blank","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2020-10-19",2020,"JP","Miyagi",2111149,"Sendai","probable",38.27,140.87,"Japan:Miyagi","blank sludge",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN24404848","0.5g/L","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2020-10-19",2020,"JP","Miyagi",2111149,"Sendai","probable",38.27,140.87,"Japan:Miyagi","0.5g/L sludge",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN24404849","1g/L","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2020-10-19",2020,"JP","Miyagi",2111149,"Sendai","probable",38.27,140.87,"Japan:Miyagi","1g/L sludge",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN